# DB Sync Defaults

Use these defaults when performing local database sync operations.

## Primary Domain Replacement

- Source: `https://www.YOUR_LIVE_DOMAIN.com`
- Target: `http://localhost:8888`
- Always include protocol downgrade (`https` -> `http`) in replacement when your local stack uses HTTP.

## API Host Replacement

- Source: `api.YOUR_LIVE_DOMAIN.com`
- Target: `api-dev.YOUR_LIVE_DOMAIN.com`

## Token Replacement

- Source: `YOUR_LIVE_TOKEN`
- Target: `YOUR_LOCAL_TOKEN`

## Required Safety Rules

1. Always back up the local DB before any import or replacement step.
2. Always run search-replace with safe flags that skip GUID updates.
3. Use network mode for multisite DB sync operations.
4. Do not sync files as part of DB sync tasks; DB only.

## Prompting Behavior

When asked to run or generate DB sync commands:

- Apply all replacements above unless the user explicitly overrides values.
- Include safe search-replace behavior (`--skip-columns=guid` or equivalent).
- Keep DB sync and file sync as separate workflows.
